1
00:00:01,879 --> 00:00:08,610
Lesson ten. Bob visits the village market. Bob goes to the village market, a supermarket

2
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:14,650
in town. He asks Carol, the owner of the store, if she would like to sell Susan's

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,129
scrumptious cookies. Carol agrees but isn't able to tell Bob how much she'll pay him.

4
00:00:20,859 --> 00:00:23,049
Thank you for making time for me today, Carol.

5
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:26,309
Don't mention it, Bob. What's up?

6
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:30,910
My wife baked these cookies from scratch. Please take one.

7
00:00:31,199 --> 00:00:34,609
Hmm, chewy. These are out of this world.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,189
My wife's a great cook.

9
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:43,629
You can say that again. I don't want to make a pig of myself, but let me take a few more.

10
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:46,170
Oink oink, just kidding.

11
00:00:47,159 --> 00:00:53,289
I'd like to sell these at the village market. My customers will go nuts over these.

12
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:56,309
How much would you pay us for each cookie?

13
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:03,549
I'm not sure. I need to roll up my sleeves and figure out the finances.

14
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,390
Can you give me a ballpark figure now?

15
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:14,350
I don't want to jump the gun. Sit tight for now and we'll talk things over this evening.

